    <item>
      <title>Brysk 0.1.0</title>
      <pubDate>Wed, 18 Nov 2026 18:38:30 GMT</pubDate>
      <sparkle:version>4</sparkle:version>
      <sparkle:shortVersionString>0.1.0</sparkle:shortVersionString>
      <sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>13.0</sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>
      <description sparkle:descriptionFormat="plain-text">Initial release of Brysk, a Rust file manager extensively reworked and extended for macOS.

- Native macOS menus, Command shortcuts, dialogs, sharing and permission onboarding.
- Tabs, split panes, multiple views, Finder-style file operations and drag previews.
- DirectLook previews for images, video, PDFs, text and archives, with sharper image loading.
- Fast name search, asynchronous listing and thumbnails, and memory/performance improvements.
- Optional Finder Dock-click replacement that works after Quit through a small background helper.
- Signed in-app updates, HyperSearch, and an optional menu-bar icon (off by default).

Download: Developer ID-signed and notarized universal DMG for Apple silicon and Intel. Requires macOS 13 or later.

Based on rustyfiles by Özer Güzel, with extensive macOS-specific changes. See the README for features and known limits.</description>
      <sparkle:fullReleaseNotesLink>https://github.com/rexmont/brysk/releases/tag/v0.1.0</sparkle:fullReleaseNotesLink>
